{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact M3 head 47fb5be4716299083f0453cba9c19391b1cfd4ce on builder/typed-core-m3-20261105, tree 66149d7e, for request f012c968 under promise 4c857d41 and review request b713c2dd. This approval covers the 52 paths at this head, including the replay fixture and Page asset paths that addendum 907088f9 names.\n\nScope. Main 93c1600b is an ancestor, the worktree is clean, and the branch is pushed. The head adds 25 commits over main, and the commit-message check passes for all 25. Production changes are limited to packages/derive/src: handlers.ts, sends.ts, program/evaluate.ts, two new modules (program/reads.ts and program/structure.ts) and ten validator files. judge.ts hashes to 86222a9f… at main and at this head. No package manifest, lockfile, Wrangler file, Native definition, grant or wire type changes. After gate commit 30ed3c98, only the note, the gate manifest and the two plan status lines change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The structural visitor is equivalent to the deleted traversals. readsClock followed before, after, anyOf, each.guards and has.guards. timesEffect added value-from-time and the effect's if and unless. conditionsReadClock added tell.if, relate.if and notify.if. The validator records each of these forms as a child of its owning node. guard, effect, send and notify each open their node before they validate their nested lists. A value effect records a commit-clock source exactly where it reads `time`. declaredClockReads counts before, after and commit-clock sources, and nothing else. A `rule` guard and a Native mark stay leaves, as they were before. The rg query for the three deleted names finds nothing in packages/derive/src or packages/derive/test.\n- Future result clauses stay separate. Each clause gets its own root with an origin link, and a send records the link without a child edge, so a parent never counts its clause's clock use. runClause selects the clause by send identity, clause name, origin root and kind. The outcome clause has no origin body, and its marks add no clock use.\n- Native clock use stays actual. Both callers OR the declared result with `j.ran?.clock`, and neither resets that flag. The Native witness shows that an absent field skips the hook with zero calls and no judgesTime, and that a present field runs it twice and refuses the behind-clock write.\n- Late replacement lookup holds. handlerBranch rebuilds the body from the same header objects, and replacementMatches compares those headers by identity and treats two empty arrays as equal. The kind filter keeps two handlers with shared header objects apart.\n- Validation keeps its decisions. Every validator change either adds recording or refactors a check into the same logic: ownerOf wraps the same lazy owner, bindElement builds the same element map plus a binding path, and the party-slot and fact-field checks read the same slot and field. No problem code, message or path changes, and canonical bytes and digests come from the unchanged declared object.\n- The witnesses show the public decisions. Each of the seven new cases pairs a clock variant with a nonclock variant and asserts `clock-behind`, a write or the clause's own judgesTime. Three controls fail exactly 5, 1 and 1 selected assertion sets, and the restored source matches checkpoint 395326e6. The first Native control's survival stays retained.\n- The gate passed. gate.exit reads exit 0 at 30ed3c98, tree 56ab5d84: Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 3,987 with one skip and Native 1,111 with two skips. All four phases are terminal and complete, and both Vitest phases report zero unhandled errors. before.json and after.json record a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43, and receipt.json shows unchanged source and no owned process left. The failed gate at cb614e2f stays retained with exit 1 and Native unreached.\n- Page browser scripts run 42183221543 concluded success at exactly 47fb5be4.\n- Evidence. The note states the SHA-256 of the gate manifest, and it matches. All 18 manifests list 306 files, and every file matches its size and digest, is read-only and holds no credential.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The graph belongs to the admitted ValidDefinition object, the validator records it during its existing calls, and both production callers read the same root that validation checked. Concrete execution keeps its route, and the graph holds no callback.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change adds no authority and reads no new input. A missing graph throws TypeError before any primitive runs, so a body that validation did not capture never derives.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes for later:\n\n1. In validate/format-1.ts, bindReads runs inside the try whose catch reports \"has no canonical bytes\". If an internal capture check in finishStructure ever throws, that message would hide the real cause. Move bindReads out of that try, or give its failure its own message.\n2. Plan 035 and notes/plans/README.md say M3 \"awaits independent review\", and the note's status says review and landing remain pending. After the landing, the planner's next head should change those lines to name the landing commit.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3ec065b9cee9c58fcc18efcc6c30a34a0110d06d","binding":"assigned","head":"47fb5be4716299083f0453cba9c19391b1cfd4ce","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:366bf3677995b6c551d9d7cd404670bec7d0fada\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9a8c08a76e966d5d13d341a5f78e49fc53bf7a9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4c857d41d38e06c8129cc24986af5486585cbc9b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d9a635d275b4fbb0ea788d6f4d75d6cbd87769e4","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}